# Create New Shipment & Package Details – UI Implementation Rule

## Objective

Build the complete UI flow for creating a new shipment, including package details and real-time quote preview, strictly following the provided user flowchart and design system.  
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (for client-side state, if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)
- **Naming & Scoping:** All new UI features, pages, and components **must** follow the rules in `@naming-and-scoping.mdc` for unique IDs, class names, and structure. This is required for easy inspection and debugging.

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Shipment Creation Flow (All UI, No Backend)
- **Create New Shipment Page:**  
  - Sender info (pre-filled, read-only)
  - Recipient info (name, address, phone)
  - Package details (weight, dimensions, type)
  - Service selection (standard, express, overnight)
  - Special instructions/notes

- **Package Details Page:**  
  - Dimensions (length, width, height)
  - Weight and unit selection
  - Package type (box, envelope, etc.)
  - Fragile/valuable item flags
  - Custom packaging requirements

- **Real-time Quote Preview:**  
  - Mock quote calculation based on form data
  - Show multiple service options with pricing
  - Estimated delivery times
  - Insurance options

- **Label Purchase Flow:**  
  - Mock payment UI (Stripe-style)
  - Order summary and confirmation
  - Payment method selection
  - Receipt/confirmation screen

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for all navigation.
- All flows must match the provided user flowchart.
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).
- "Create New Shipment" button on dashboard must route to this flow.

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for quotes, service options, and confirmation.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.
- **All new UI features, pages, and components must follow the rules in `@naming-and-scoping.mdc` for IDs and class names.**

---

## 6. Deliverables

- All pages and components for the shipment creation flow.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running and testing the shipment flow.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file, `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`, and all referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern shipment creation UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

